ictions, return an empty JSON FILE {}\n- The entire text of the eligibility criteria must be included and separated by the logical operators, without omitting any words or information.\n- The output should only contain the JSON object, without any additional text or formatting.\n- Ensure that the JSON output strictly follows these rules and accurately represents the logical structure of the input eligibility criteria.\n\n### Input:\n-  Diagnosis of COPD confirmed by clinical examination and a pulmonary function test\n-  Stable clinical condition (without recent respiratory system infections or any exacerbation of the disease)\n-  Patients must be willing to re evaluate at the end of the study\n-  Patients must be willing to give written consent for their participation in the study\n\n### Response:\n{\n  "AND": {\n    "left": {\n      "AND": {\n        "left": {\n          "AND": {\n            "left": {\n              "AND": {\n                "left": {\n                  "raw_text": "- Diagnosis of COPD confirmed by clinical examination",\n                  "Condition": [\n                    "COPD"\n                  ],\n                  "Condition-Name": [\n                    "COPD"\n                  ],\n                  "Procedure": [\n                    "clinical examination"\n                  ],\n                  "Procedure-Name": [\n                    "clinical examination"\n                  ]\n                },\n                "right": {\n                  "raw_text": "and a pulmonary function test",\n                  "Observation": [\n                    "pulmonary function test"\n                  ],\n                  "Observation-Name": [\n                    "pulmonary function test"\n                  ]\n                }\n              }\n            },\n            "right": {\n              "AND": {\n                "left": {\n                  "raw_text": "- Stable clinical condition (",\n                  "Condition": [\n               