ictions, return an empty JSON FILE {}\n- The entire text of the eligibility criteria must be included and separated by the logical operators, without omitting any words or information.\n- The output should only contain the JSON object, without any additional text or formatting.\n- Ensure that the JSON output strictly follows these rules and accurately represents the logical structure of the input eligibility criteria.\n\n### Input:\n1. Moderate-severe uni- and bipolar depression according to the International Classification of Diseases (ICD-10)\n2. A Hamilton scale score (HDS-17) of ≥ 18 and/or a sub-scale (HDSS) score of ≥ 9 within 24-48 hours before the first treatment\n\n### Response:\n{\n  "AND": {\n    "left": {\n      "OR": {\n        "left": {\n          "raw_text": "1. Moderate-severe uni-",\n          "Severity": [\n            "Moderate",\n            "severe"\n          ],\n          "Modifier": [\n            "uni"\n          ]\n        },\n        "right": {\n          "raw_text": "and bipolar depression according to the International Classification of Diseases (ICD-10)",\n          "Condition": [\n            "depression"\n          ],\n          "Condition-Name": [\n            "depression"\n          ],\n          "Modifier": [\n            "bipolar"\n          ]\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    "right": {\n      "OR": {\n        "left": {\n          "raw_text": "2. A Hamilton scale score (HDS-17) of ≥ 18",\n          "Eq-Operator": [\n            "≥"\n          ],\n          "Eq-Value": [\n            "18",\n            "17"\n          ],\n          "Eq-Comparison": [\n            "≥ 18"\n          ],\n          "Observation": [\n            "Hamilton scale score",\n            "HDS-17"\n          ],\n          "Observation-Name": [\n            "Hamilton scale score",\n            "HDS-17"\n          ]\n        },\n        "right": {\n          "raw_text": "and/or a sub-scale (HDSS) score of ≥ 9 within 24-48 hours before the first treatment",\n    