ictions, return an empty JSON FILE {}\n- The entire text of the eligibility criteria must be included and separated by the logical operators, without omitting any words or information.\n- The output should only contain the JSON object, without any additional text or formatting.\n- Ensure that the JSON output strictly follows these rules and accurately represents the logical structure of the input eligibility criteria.\n\n### Input:\n1. Patients with atrial fibrillation/ arrhythmias.\n2. Within 2 weeks of cardiac catheterization or arterial puncture at femoral puncture site.\n3. Decompensated heart failure, usually class 3 or 4\n4. LV EF <30%\n5. Moderate or severe AR\n6. Persistent and uncontrolled hypertension (BP persistently >160/100 mmHg)\n7. Bleeding diathesis\n8. Active thrombophlebitis/ venous disease of lower limbs\n9. Severe lower extremity vaso-occlusive disease\n10. Presence of a documented aortic aneurysm/ dissection requiring surgical repair\n11. Pregnancy\n\n### Response:\n{\n  "AND": {\n    "left": {\n      "AND": {\n        "left": {\n          "AND": {\n            "left": {\n              "AND": {\n                "left": {\n                  "AND": {\n                    "left": {\n                      "AND": {\n                        "left": {\n                          "AND": {\n                            "left": {\n                              "AND": {\n                                "left": {\n                                  "AND": {\n                                    "left": {\n                                      "AND": {\n                                        "left": {\n                                          "AND": {\n                                            "left": {\n                                              "AND": {\n                                                "left": {\n                                                  "AND": {\n                                                    "left": {\n                    