ictions, return an empty JSON FILE {}\n- The entire text of the eligibility criteria must be included and separated by the logical operators, without omitting any words or information.\n- The output should only contain the JSON object, without any additional text or formatting.\n- Ensure that the JSON output strictly follows these rules and accurately represents the logical structure of the input eligibility criteria.\n\n### Input:\n-  Any condition that might prevent the father\'s infant from reaching normal developmental milestones will participation, including congenital malformations or prematurity requiring prolonged/ ongoing infant hospitalization.\n\n### Response:\n{\n  "OR": {\n    "left": {\n      "raw_text": "- Any condition that might prevent the father\'s infant from reaching normal developmental milestones will participation, including congenital malformations",\n      "Condition": [\n        "congenital malformations"\n      ],\n      "Condition-Name": [\n        "congenital malformations"\n      ],\n      "Family-Member": [\n        "father\'s infant"\n      ],\n      "Observation": [\n        "developmental milestones"\n      ],\n      "Observation-Name": [\n        "developmental milestones"\n      ],\n      "Polarity": [\n        "normal"\n      ],\n      "Condition-Type": [\n        "prevent"\n      ],\n      "Assertion": [\n        "might"\n      ]\n    },\n    "right": {\n      "raw_text": "or prematurity requiring prolonged/ ongoing infant hospitalization.",\n      "Condition": [\n        "prematurity"\n      ],\n      "Condition-Name": [\n        "prematurity"\n      ],\n      "Family-Member": [\n        "infant"\n      ],\n      "Encounter": [\n        "hospitalization"\n      ],\n      "Acuteness": [\n        "prolonged",\n        "ongoing"\n      ]\n    }\n  }\n}<|eot_id|>']
