ictions, return an empty JSON FILE {}\n- The entire text of the eligibility criteria must be included and separated by the logical operators, without omitting any words or information.\n- The output should only contain the JSON object, without any additional text or formatting.\n- Ensure that the JSON output strictly follows these rules and accurately represents the logical structure of the input eligibility criteria.\n\n### Input:\n-  the emergency departments assessment of a critical clinical condition oppose an examination with both modalities (ULDCT of the chest, chest X-ray)\n-  assigned to chest X-ray as follow-up\n-  women with positive ß-HCG-test\n\n### Response:\n{\n  "AND": {\n    "left": {\n      "AND": {\n        "left": {\n          "AND": {\n            "left": {\n              "raw_text": "- the emergency departments assessment of a critical clinical condition oppose an examination with both modalities (ULDCT of the chest, chest X-ray)",\n              "Condition": [\n                "clinical condition"\n              ],\n              "Condition-Name": [\n                "clinical condition"\n              ],\n              "Procedure": [\n                "ULDCT of the chest",\n                "chest X-ray"\n              ],\n              "Procedure-Name": [\n                "ULDCT of the chest",\n                "chest X-ray"\n              ],\n              "Location": [\n                "emergency departments"\n              ],\n              "Severity": [\n                "critical"\n              ],\n              "Assertion": [\n                "oppose"\n              ]\n            },\n            "right": {\n              "raw_text": "- assigned to chest X-ray as follow-up",\n              "Procedure": [\n                "chest X-ray"\n              ],\n              "Procedure-Name": [\n                "chest X-ray"\n              ],\n              "Encounter": [\n                "follow-up"\n              ]\n            }\n          }\n  