ictions, return an empty JSON FILE {}\n- The entire text of the eligibility criteria must be included and separated by the logical operators, without omitting any words or information.\n- The output should only contain the JSON object, without any additional text or formatting.\n- Ensure that the JSON output strictly follows these rules and accurately represents the logical structure of the input eligibility criteria.\n\n### Input:\n-  Effort oxygen therapy\n-  Cardiovascular, neuromuscular or musculoskeletal disorders that can provide significant dyspnea or limit exercise\n-  Legal incapacity\n-  Low or no cooperation anticipated\n\n### Response:\n{\n  "AND": {\n    "left": {\n      "AND": {\n        "left": {\n          "AND": {\n            "left": {\n              "raw_text": "- Effort oxygen therapy",\n              "Procedure": [\n                "oxygen therapy"\n              ],\n              "Procedure-Name": [\n                "oxygen therapy"\n              ],\n              "Modifier": [\n                "Effort"\n              ]\n            },\n            "right": {\n              "OR": {\n                "left": {\n                  "raw_text": "- Cardiovascular,",\n                  "Modifier": [\n                    "Cardiovascular"\n                  ]\n                },\n                "right": {\n                  "OR": {\n                    "left": {\n                      "raw_text": "neuromuscular",\n                      "Modifier": [\n                        "neuromuscular"\n                      ]\n                    },\n                    "right": {\n                      "OR": {\n                        "left": {\n                          "raw_text": "or musculoskeletal disorders that can provide significant dyspnea",\n                          "Condition": [\n                            "disorders",\n                            "dyspnea"\n                          ],\n                          "Condition-Name": [\n               