ictions, return an empty JSON FILE {}\n- The entire text of the eligibility criteria must be included and separated by the logical operators, without omitting any words or information.\n- The output should only contain the JSON object, without any additional text or formatting.\n- Ensure that the JSON output strictly follows these rules and accurately represents the logical structure of the input eligibility criteria.\n\n### Input:\n-  Women called back from a screening mammography by either FFDM or tomosynthesis with soft tissue abnormalities including masses, asymmetries, focal asymmetries or architectural distortion with or without calcifications. Patients will be questioned regarding the possibility of pregnancy and will need a negative pregnancy test prior the study intervention.\n\n### Response:\n{\n  "AND": {\n    "left": {\n      "raw_text": "- Women called back from a screening mammography by either FFDM or tomosynthesis with soft tissue abnormalities including masses, asymmetries, focal asymmetries or architectural distortion",\n      "Procedure": [\n        "mammography",\n        "FFDM",\n        "tomosynthesis",\n        "screening mammography"\n      ],\n      "Procedure-Name": [\n        "mammography",\n        "FFDM",\n        "tomosynthesis",\n        "screening mammography"\n      ],\n      "Condition": [\n        "soft tissue abnormalities",\n        "masses",\n        "asymmetries",\n        "focal asymmetries",\n        "architectural distortion"\n      ],\n      "Condition-Name": [\n        "soft tissue abnormalities",\n        "masses",\n        "asymmetries",\n        "focal asymmetries",\n        "architectural distortion"\n      ],\n      "Life-Stage-And-Gender": [\n        "Women"\n      ]\n    },\n    "right": {\n      "raw_text": "with or without calcifications. Patients will be questioned regarding the possibility of pregnancy and will need a negative pregnancy test prior the study intervention.",\n      "Condition": [\n        "calcifi